  <!--
    IMPORTANT CAVEAT — READ BEFORE RELYING ON THIS DOCUMENT:
    This manifest declares the LOGICAL append-only / immutability
    guarantees of the worm-pow-rsa record format (hash-chain linkage via
    prev_hash/record_hash, RFC 8785 JCS canonicalization, SHA-256 hashing,
    and optional PoW sealing). These guarantees mean that if a record is
    altered or removed after the fact, that tampering is DETECTABLE by
    re-verifying the chain.

    This XML metadata does NOT, by itself, PREVENT tampering. XML files on
    an ordinary writable filesystem can be edited, replaced, or deleted
    like any other file. Genuine write-once/read-many enforcement — actual
    prevention, not just detection — requires a physical or platform-level
    control independent of this document, such as:
      - Object storage in compliance/governance WORM lock mode
        (e.g. S3 Object Lock, Azure Immutable Blob Storage)
      - Write-once optical/tape media
      - A permissioned, replicated append-only log service
      - OS-level immutability flags combined with restricted write access
        and independent audit of the enforcing host

    See append_only_guarantees/physical_worm_enforcement below for whether
    such a control is actually configured for THIS deployment; it defaults
    to false until an operator wires one up and sets it explicitly.
  -->
  <wm:append_only_guarantees>
    <wm:hash_chain_linkage>true</wm:hash_chain_linkage>
    <wm:pow_sealed>true</wm:pow_sealed>
    <wm:canonicalization>RFC8785-JCS</wm:canonicalization>
    <wm:hash_algorithm>SHA-256</wm:hash_algorithm>
    <wm:physical_worm_enforcement>false</wm:physical_worm_enforcement>
    <wm:physical_enforcement_mechanism>none configured — local filesystem storage backend only</wm:physical_enforcement_mechanism>
    <wm:caveat>XML metadata in this manifest alone does NOT provide physical WORM enforcement. Genuine write-once/immutability guarantees require storage-layer controls independent of this document.</wm:caveat>
  </wm:append_only_guarantees>

</wm:worm_manifest>
